From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:21:24 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: let the core suspend after a reset

rocket_reset() drops the in-flight job's runtime PM reference with
pm_runtime_put_noidle(), which requests nothing, so the core does not
suspend until something else asks and its power domain does not cycle. On
RK3576 the domain's power-on resets the NPU bus interface; without it the
IOMMU stops answering and the job after a timeout fails.

Use pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(), as the completion path does. On a ROCK 4D
the job after a timeout goes from 0 to 128 of 128 channels correct.

Also drop the runtime PM reference after rocket_core_reset(), so the NPU
core stays powered during the reset.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260819073530.6087-1-royalnet026@gmail.com/
Fixes: 0810d5ad88a1 ("accel/rocket: Add job submission IOCTL")
Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Reviewed-by: Heiko Stuebner <heiko@sntech.de>
Tested-by: Sidong Yang <sidong.yang@furiosa.ai> # RK3588, ROCK 5B+
Reviewed-by: Tomeu Vizoso <tomeu@tomeuvizoso.net>
Signed-off-by: Tomeu Vizoso <tomeu@tomeuvizoso.net>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/2afd051e37b8dd4f10e347a3537b0086973d554c.1794615323.git.gahing@gahingwoo.com
[carried for the RK3576 series as upstream 36161ff0c00f. The merged commit
 drops the RK3576 rationale above; it holds here, where 0003 makes the
 domain's power-on cycle the bus interface reset. Dropped when the base
 carries 36161ff0c00f.]
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index aa218331de6..7634a17ff20 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -780,6 +780,8 @@ static void rocket_job_handle_irq(struct rocket_core *core, bool from_poll)
 static void
 rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 {
+	bool put_job_ref;
+
 	if (!atomic_read(&core->reset.pending))
 		return;
 
@@ -867,13 +869,13 @@ rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 	synchronize_irq(core->irq);
 
 	/*
-	 * No handler is running now, but we might still have stuck jobs. Let's
-	 * make sure the PM counters stay balanced by manually calling
-	 * pm_runtime_put_noidle().
+	 * No handler is running now, but we might still have stuck jobs. Take
+	 * the job's runtime PM reference over from it, and keep it until the
+	 * core has been reset: the reference is what keeps the power domain up
+	 * while that happens.
 	 */
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &core->job_lock) {
-		if (core->in_flight_job)
-			pm_runtime_put_noidle(core->dev);
+		put_job_ref = core->in_flight_job;
 
 		/*
 		 * The reset wipes the IOMMU page-table base, so drop the
@@ -893,6 +895,13 @@ rocket_reset(struct rocket_core *core, struct drm_sched_job *bad)
 	/* Proceed with reset now. */
 	rocket_core_reset(core);
 
+	/*
+	 * Balance the PM counters now that the core has been reset, and
+	 * request idle while doing it so the core can suspend.
+	 */
+	if (put_job_ref)
+		pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
+
 	/* NPU has been reset, we can clear the reset pending bit. */
 	atomic_set(&core->reset.pending, 0);
 
-- 
